<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan July M2 money supply up 8.47 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan July M2 money supply up 8.47 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-08-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's broadest money supply measure, M2, grew 8.47 percent in July from a year earlier after rising 8.50 percent in June, the central bank said on Saturday.  </p>
<p>			   July 1996	  June 1996</p>
<p> M2 ANNUAL RATE	    +8.47	     +8.50</p>
<p> M1B ANNUAL RATE	   +5.80	     +5.55</p>
<p> M1A ANNUAL RATE	   +1.68	     +0.92</p>
<p>The central bank target for M2 growth is 9-14 percent.</p>
<p>Note - M1A is cash, checking accounts and passbook deposits. M1B is M1A plus savings accounts. M2 is M1B plus quasi-money.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
